                            Installation

To install YatZ, copy YatZ.app it to any directory (like \APP\) and
install it <Psion-I> from the system screen.  Alternatively, rename it
YatZ.img, and copy it to the \IMG\ directory, or any other directory
(such as a games alias) referenced by an alias of RunImg.

It was written with the SIBO 'C' SDK.  Source is in the src.zip archive,
or, if it wasn't included in the distribution, obtainable from the author.


                               Credits

I got the idea after ftp'ing a version for the Amiga, and remembered
how we used to play it a lot as kids.  I only look at the Amiga source
code once to check the bonus threshold, but it was fun to play the Amiga
version.


                                Rules

The object of the game is to score as many points as possible by
scoring in thirteen different categories.  Five dice are rolled.  The
player then chooses to roll up to five of the dice two more times.  Once
a hand is scored, all the dice are rolled again and the process is
repeated.

After any roll, the player can score the hand.  Each category
can only be used once in a game.  If the hand does not fit into
any category then the player is forced to scratch an unused
category with zero score.  If he/she is force to scratch a yachtzee,
then no more yachtzees may be scored.

Category <key>:        Score:

1 <1> (ones)           total of all dice with 1 showing
2 <2> (twos)           total of all dice with 2 showing
3 <3> (threes)         total of all dice with 3 showing
4 <4> (fours)          total of all dice with 4 showing
5 <5> (fives)          total of all dice with 5 showing
6 <6> (sixes)          total of all dice with 6 showing

If the total score in the above categories is greater then 62
then an additional bonus score of 35 is added.

Three of a kind <t>    total of all dice (if three of a kind)
Four of a kind <f>     total of all dice (if four of a kind)
full House <h>         25 (three of a kind and a pair)
Small straight <s>     30 (four dice in sequence)
Large straight <l>     40 (five dice in sequence)
Chance <c>             total of all dice
Yachtzee <y>           50

e.g.

First roll:
 1  3  4  6  6  - Keep the sixes

Second Roll:
 6  5  2  6  6  - Keep the sixes
	
Third Roll:
 6  6  1  6  6  - Score either four of a kind (25) or four sixes (24)

When all of the categories have been used the game is over and the
score is totalled.


                              Controls

<Left> and <Right> move the highlighting box.
<Space> toggles the highlighted die.
<Enter> rerolls all showing dice.
Keys listed above score in a particular category.


                              Compiling

YatZ was written completely with PLIB, HWIF, and WLIB functions, and
as such is not portable (even to other SIBO machines, unless you want
to rewrite all the HWIF sections) in any way.  See the src.zip archive
for all files necessary to recompile.

There is only one real compilation option (for debugging):

If you #define WIZARD_MODE and recompile:  During play, pressing the
key <w> will allow you to change the current die.


